{
  id:"granit", title:"OPERATION “GRANITE”", tech:"Rocking from Both Sides", badge:"ROCKING", node:"GRANITE", art:"assets/op_granit.png", map:{x:26,y:48},
  brief:"The outlet Spotlight published an investigation into non-combat deaths of recruits at training centers of the “Granite” assault regiment: dozens of witnesses, documents, grim details. The State Bureau of Investigation opened a case, the commander was suspended pending review. The feed has split in two, and both halves are screaming. Your shift started an hour ago.",
  attack:-14,
  feed:[
    {osint:{created:"Outlet has been operating for 9 years.", postsMonth:"60+ pieces published per month.", avatar:"Editorial logo, unchanged.", nameHistory:"Unchanged.", oldPosts:["“Investigation into defense procurement,” a year ago","“How wounded evacuation works: a report”","“Who funds the rehabilitation centers”"], repostedBy:"Major media outlets, journalist communities, international correspondents."}, a:"🔦 Spotlight, editorial team", t:"Our investigation: at least 26 non-combat deaths in the “Granite” regiment's training centers over the past six months. More than 30 witnesses, medical records, testimony from families. The regiment gave no substantive response. Full story at the link.", m:"09:00", v:"187K", h:false,
     w:"An inconvenient truth isn't disinformation. An investigation with sources, documents, and a right of reply is a self-cleaning mechanism, not a hostile narrative. Flag it, and you've done exactly what the enemy wants: killed your own society's immune system."},
    {osint:{created:"Official regiment channel, 2023.", postsMonth:"20 posts per month.", avatar:"Regiment emblem.", nameHistory:"Unchanged.", oldPosts:["“Report on operations in the sector”","“EW-equipment fundraiser closed in a day, thank you”","“Our crews commended by command”"], repostedBy:"Military channels, support communities."}, a:"🪨 “Granite” Regiment, official", t:"Most of those mentioned in the piece died in hospitals from illness, not at training centers. Some of the “witnesses” have disciplinary records and a history of unauthorized absence. We ask that no conclusions be drawn on our behalf.", m:"10:15", v:"94K", h:false,
     w:"Bad, damaging communication, but it's ours, not the enemy's. “Died in hospitals” doesn't explain how they got there, and a witness's disciplinary record doesn't prove they lied. This is a press-office failure the enemy will now pick apart for quotes. Your own side's incompetence is a problem to fix, not a target to flag."},
    {osint:{created:"Channel registered 5 months ago.", postsMonth:"70 posts per month, sharp spike this week.", avatar:"Stock image of a broken chevron patch.", nameHistory:"“Trench Truth” → “Truth About the Army,” renamed a month ago.", oldPosts:["“What draft roundups really cost”","“Why commanders don't care about losses”","“Stories of those who got out”"], repostedBy:"The same anonymous aggregators that spread Insider UA and Prawda Bez Cenzury."}, a:"💀 Truth About the Army", t:"26 bodies before the front line even started. Think about it: commanders are killing more than the occupiers are. And that's just one regiment, there are hundreds. Who's defending an army like that? Every draft notice is now a lottery with your life.", m:"10:40", v:"142K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Generalization"},
    {osint:{created:"Profile registered 8 months ago.", postsMonth:"25 posts per month, all about media and “paid-for pieces.”", avatar:"Photo of a person in glasses, stock in origin.", nameHistory:"Bio changed: “media analyst” → “information hygiene expert.”", oldPosts:["“Who pays for high-profile investigations”","“Anatomy of a paid media hit piece”","“Why you can't trust fact-checkers”"], repostedBy:"“Alternative analysis” channels and the same aggregators as “Truth About the Army.”"}, a:"🧐 Media Hygiene", t:"Quietly, no emotion. Spotlight's editorial team has ALREADY admitted an error on one of the names on the list. One proven error. How many more unproven ones are there? A piece where fabrication has been found isn't called an investigation. It's called something else.", m:"11:20", v:"88K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"Source Poisoning"},
    {osint:{created:"Channel registered 3 weeks ago.", postsMonth:"55 posts in three weeks of existence.", avatar:"Flag with a sword, AI-generated image.", nameHistory:"Unchanged.", oldPosts:["No posts before this week — the channel launched straight into the “stab in the army's back” topic."], repostedBy:"The same anonymous aggregators as “Truth About the Army” and “Media Hygiene.”"}, a:"⚔️ The Rear Won't Betray", t:"While the “Granite” guys are holding the line, journalists are stabbing them in the back for a paycheck. Time to call it what it is: these “investigators” are the enemy's second front. Remember these names. They will answer for this.", m:"12:05", v:"116K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"Patriotic Wrapper"},
    {osint:{created:"Profile registered in 2018.", postsMonth:"4 posts per month, personal.", avatar:"Family photo.", nameHistory:"Unchanged.", oldPosts:["“Son took the oath, so proud”","“Sent a care package to the training ground”","“Does anyone know how to reach the unit?”"], repostedBy:"Relatives, local communities."}, a:"👵 A Recruit's Mother", t:"my son was there. he called once a week, said “everything's fine, mom,” but his voice wasn't his. i want the truth. not against the army, no. against hiding from me what happened to my child", m:"12:30", v:"64K", h:false,
     w:"The hardest trap in the feed. The pain is real, the demand for truth is legitimate, there's no hostile framing here at all. Flag a grieving mother, and a screenshot of your “moderation” becomes fuel for both hostile pipelines at once."},
    {osint:{created:"Official channel, 2022.", postsMonth:"25 posts per month.", avatar:"State emblem.", nameHistory:"Unchanged.", oldPosts:["“Report on the results of a unit inspection”","“Clarification on servicemembers' rights”","“Schedule for receiving inquiries from families”"], repostedBy:"Government channels, human rights organizations, media."}, a:"🏛 Office of the Military Ombudsman", t:"An inspection has been opened based on the facts in the publication. The regiment commander has been suspended for the duration of the investigation. An interagency commission is at work. Every case is being reviewed individually, and inquiries from families are accepted around the clock.", m:"13:10", v:"71K", h:false,
     w:"An institutional response: inspection, suspension, a channel for families. This isn't a narrative, it's the system doing its job. And that's exactly what the enemy is trying to make invisible."},
    {osint:{created:"Profile registered in 2022.", postsMonth:"12 posts per month, from the front line.", avatar:"Pixelated photo, face not shown.", nameHistory:"Callsign unchanged.", oldPosts:["“Hit on target, drone footage”","“Thanks for the supplies, the guys are alive”","“Three days with no rotation, holding on”"], repostedBy:"Fellow soldiers, military channels."}, a:"🎖 Callsign “Krok,” “Granite” soldier", t:"i'm on the zero line right now reading all of this. if what they're writing about happened at the training center, the guilty need to go to prison, and i'll be the first to sign off on that. but don't lump us, the ones here, in with what's being investigated. we're not “bodies before the front.” we're a regiment.", m:"13:45", v:"103K", h:false,
     w:"A genuine soldier's take: demands accountability AND refuses generalization at the same time. This isn't a narrative, it's a ready-made counter-narrative that grew on its own. Smart counter-play amplifies voices like this, it doesn't moderate them."}
  ],
  techniques:{
    q:"“Truth About the Army” shouts that commanders are killers. “The Rear Won't Betray” shouts that journalists are traitors. They're shouting opposite things. What's actually going on here?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Rocking from Both Sides", d:"Both pipelines — “the army kills its own” and “journalists are enemy agents” — are driven by one enemy", ok:true,
       e:"Exactly. Look at the OSINT: channels shouting opposite things get reposted by the same aggregators. The enemy doesn't care which side you're on. It needs you to think in “sides” at all, in a place where the army is fighting, the investigation is working, and journalism is doing its job. Three processes, zero contradictions, until someone draws a front line between them."},
      {n:"Source Poisoning", d:"One corrected editorial error gets inflated into “the whole piece is fabricated”", ok:false,
       e:"That's how “Media Hygiene” operates, and it's the subtlest link in the chain. But it's one wing of the scheme, not the whole scheme. The other wing is poisoning trust in the opposite direction at the same time. See only one wing, and you've missed the attack."},
      {n:"Parasitizing a Conflict", d:"A real scandal gets pumped up with a fabricated layer, like in the border case", ok:false,
       e:"Close, but no. At the border there was a real conflict between two sides with real interests. Here there's no conflict: the investigation, the army, and the inspection aren't at war with each other. The enemy isn't parasitizing a front line, it's drawing one where none existed."},
      {n:"Appeal to betrayal", d:"“Commanders don't care about their people,” “journalists stabbed us in the back” — it all revolves around betrayal", ok:false,
       e:"Betrayal is the fuel for both pipelines, that's true. But fuel isn't the scheme. The scheme is that “traitor” gets pinned on the army one moment and the media the next, from a single source. The label changes, the rupture stays."}
    ]
  },
  counters:{
    q:"Both pipelines are already at full speed, Spotlight is getting threats, the regiment is getting curses. Your move:",
    opts:[
      {n:"Split the tracks publicly", d:"Three points: the investigation is underway; the regiment isn't the individuals; journalism did its job. Amplify Krok's voice.", fx:12, best:true,
       e:"Surgery against the rocking: show that the three processes don't contradict each other, and that the front line between them was drawn from outside. A soldier's voice from the zero line is worth more here than ten official statements, it can't be filed under “traitor” or “paid shill.”"},
      {n:"Stay silent until the investigation concludes", d:"Any comment right now risks pressuring the investigation and feeding the story. Wait for the official results, then give one full position.", fx:3, cons:true, best:false,
       e:"The investigation needs months. The pipelines need hours. While you stay silent, “killer commanders” and “traitor journalists” become common knowledge, and your future conclusions will be read through that lens. Loud silence in its purest form."},
      {n:"Declare the investigation a hostile info op", d:"Publicly claim it's a plant commissioned by the enemy, demand the piece be taken down and the editorial team formally investigated.", fx:-12, rep:-15, best:false,
       e:"You just personally carried out the second pipeline's program, “journalists are enemy agents” now comes from an official mouth. Bonus: nobody will be able to debunk the next real hostile info op, because you already poisoned the word “investigation” yourself."}
    ]
  },
  debrief:"Rocking from both sides is the enemy's most expensive scheme: two pipelines, opposite slogans, one goal, sever the link between society, the army, and the media. You recognize it not by content but by infrastructure: opposite claims, shared aggregators. The counter is to refuse to draw a front line: back the investigation, separate the regiment from the individuals under scrutiny, defend journalism's right to do its job. And remember posts 1 and 2: an inconvenient truth isn't the enemy, and your own side's bad communication isn't a narrative.",
  cliff:"Insider UA has started teasing “procurement documents.” You'd recognize the handwriting anywhere. Looks like they're building up to something big."
}
