{
  id:"sykhiv", title:"SYKHIV", tech:"Emotional Amplification", badge:"AMPLIFICATION", node:"SYKHIV", art:"assets/op_sykhiv.png", map:{x:15,y:40},
  brief:"On July 8, a clash broke out in Lviv's Sykhiv district between local residents and TCC staff. Residents reportedly blocked a TCC service minibus, damaged it, and eventually flipped it over. Video of the clash is already spreading online.",
  attack:-12,
  feed:[
    {osint:{created:"2013", postsMonth:"5-6 posts a day", avatar:"personal photo", nameHistory:"unchanged", oldPosts:["The war party covers for its own","NSDC sanctions used to wipe out the opposition","Another terrible night in Ukraine. Air defense has nothing left to shoot with."], repostedBy:"anonymous aggregators, Russian Telegram channels, a few opposition politicians"}, a:"📢 Ihor Veresiuk, political commentator, former MP", t:"Lviv. Sykhiv. Tonight police used force and gunfire to crush Ukrainians who rose up against TCC manhunters and their lawless bs… people detained!!", m:"Tue 23:50", v:"78K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Fabricated Escalation"},
    {osint:{created:"2022", postsMonth:"20-30 posts a day", avatar:"channel logo", nameHistory:"unchanged", oldPosts:["Kyiv on the brink of a humanitarian catastrophe.","A quick rundown of the Trump-Zelensky meeting","By this fall, gas prices in Ukraine will top 100 UAH a liter."], repostedBy:"Z-channels, Russian media,"}, a:"📡 The Real Deal", t:"Bankova is pulling every lever to downplay the Lviv pogrom against the TCC. Their tame opinion leaders excused the TCC's actions, then the ombudsman jumped in to condemn peaceful citizens. Simple reason - the government's scared of a third Maidan, and this war is good business for Western sponsors.", m:"Wed 08:20", v:"112K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Conspiracy Framing"},
    {osint:{created:"2022, by journalist Volodymyr Malyna", postsMonth:"15-30 posts a day", avatar:"personal photo", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["Ukraine opens weapons production in Denmark","Will this war ever end?","Government drafts changes to the 2026 state budget"], repostedBy:"news aggregators, bloggers, independent journalists"}, a:"🖋 Raspberry Cordial", t:"What happened in Lviv is the logical result of the Ministry of Defense's utterly impotent communication strategy. All these years, the state never managed to set clear rules of the game, so now it's stuck fighting its own people in the streets.", m:"Wed 09:15", v:"54K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"Insinuation"},
    {osint:{created:"in office since 2006", postsMonth:"20-30 posts a month", avatar:"personal photo", nameHistory:"unchanged", oldPosts:["Our favorite segment, “Before and After.”","A new sculpture has found a home in Stryiskyi Park","Over €2.5 million and six new deals for Lviv ahead of URC2026"], repostedBy:"News aggregators, opinion leaders."}, a:"🏛 Andriy Sadovyi, Mayor of Lviv", t:"What we saw in Lviv yesterday is very bad. Not yet a diagnosis, but already a symptom. 58,000 Lviv residents are at the front right now. Every day we bury fellow residents who didn't come home. The city gives up the lion's share of its budget to support Ukraine's Defense Forces. A group's shameful behavior can't destroy our community's reputation, but it cast a shadow over it. Right now, Russia's biggest interest is getting Ukrainians to turn on each other. Any internal conflict instantly becomes a weapon for enemy propaganda.", m:"Wed 10:00", v:"65K", h:false,
     w:"The mayor openly condemns the riot and immediately warns against internal conflict as a tool of hostile propaganda — this pushes back on the narrative, it doesn't feed it."},
    {osint:{created:"Telegram channel created in 2024.", postsMonth:"irregular", avatar:"official personal photo (in his office)", nameHistory:"changed several times to match career milestones", oldPosts:["Ukraine is finally breaking ground on the Revolution of Dignity Museum.","Bringing our people home is always the result of many agencies working in sync.","Today is Historical and Cultural Heritage Day."], repostedBy:"News aggregators, military and political commentators, international media"}, a:"🎖 Kyrylo Budanov, Head of the Presidential Office", t:"If you're tearing the clothes off and beating a soldier of your own army today, think about who's going to defend you tomorrow from an enemy army that will do the same to you - tear your clothes off, beat you. I expect a fair response from law enforcement to what happened in Lviv.", m:"Wed 10:40", v:"58K", h:false,
     w:"The post calls for a lawful response from law enforcement, not mob justice or escalation — an official, measured position."},
    {osint:{created:"2022", postsMonth:"Very high, real-time updates 24/7.", avatar:"Classic white BBC logo", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["The Kremlin is starting to grasp how tough its position in the war against Ukraine really is","Scientists accidentally discover the first dinosaur bone found in Antarctica.","EU protection for Ukrainians may be extended to 2028 - but not for some men."], repostedBy:"Major Ukrainian media, military commentators and analytical outlets, BBC Russian Service"}, a:"📰 BBC Ukraine", t:"On the evening of July 8, a serious clash broke out in Lviv between the TCC and local residents during a mobilization operation. During the confrontation, the crowd flipped over and damaged a TCC service vehicle.", m:"Tue 21:35", v:"145K", h:false,
     w:"A dry statement of fact (the flipped vehicle, the clash) with no judgment calls about gunfire or the scale of any “uprising.”"},
    {osint:{created:"2003", postsMonth:"Round-the-clock broadcasting, 24/7", avatar:"official logo", nameHistory:"Originally built on the base of TRK “NBM” and “Express-Inform”; has operated continuously as “Channel 5” since 2003.", oldPosts:["Ukraine risks losing €67M in EU aid over the State Financial Monitoring Service","Two underground poker clubs busted in Kyiv","Civil society groups launch a flash-mob campaign against Stefanchuk's new Civil Code"], repostedBy:"media tied to one oligarch's holding, military and veteran communities, regional news outlets and aggregators"}, a:"📺 Channel 5", t:"Chanting “Shame!”, they flipped a TCC vehicle: a major clash broke out in Lviv during a mobilization operation.", m:"Tue 22:10", v:"48K", h:false,
     w:"A straightforward account of the clash, without inflating its scale or blaming the authorities."},
    {osint:{created:"1957", postsMonth:"Round-the-clock broadcasting, 24/7", avatar:"white “SUSPILNE LVIV” wordmark", nameHistory:"Originally Lviv Television Studio, then TRK 'Lviv' (Channel 12), later 'UA: LVIV'; consistently 'Suspilne Lviv' since 2022.", oldPosts:["Two injured in car accident in Lviv region","Methadone hidden in kids' clothing: 34-year-old Lviv man sentenced to three years","Dnipro resident suspected of selling live ammo online in Lviv region"], repostedBy:"national media, official government bodies, city aggregator pages and bloggers"}, a:"🎙 Suspilne Lviv", t:"Clash during a call-up notification operation in Lviv's Sykhiv district: people flipped a TCC service vehicle. “They beat him, dragged him into the van and took off. People rioted. We started blocking the road so they'd bring the kid back home. They keep promising to bring him back, but it's been two hours now and still nothing... I'm sick of how people get treated. There's a law, there are rules. Nobody has the right to throw a kid in a van and haul them off.” - says eyewitness Olya.", m:"Tue 22:45", v:"52K", h:false,
     w:"Direct testimony from an eyewitness about one specific incident, with no generalizing about an “uprising” or state blame."},
    {osint:{created:"1933", postsMonth:"Very high, daily updates with analysis, global rankings, and world news.", avatar:"Official logo. Blue rectangle with large white “U.S. News” lettering.", nameHistory:"Originally the magazines “U.S. News” and “World Report”; has operated continuously under the merged U.S. News & World Report brand since 1948.", oldPosts:["The 10 leading causes of death in America in 2025","Serious stomach illnesses are spreading across the US.","Photos: The War in Ukraine"], repostedBy:"International news aggregators and global media, leading Ukrainian outlets"}, a:"🌐 US News & World Report", t:"Clashes in Lviv underscore wartime tensions over military conscription.", m:"Wed 14:20", v:"22K", h:false,
     w:"A general analytical point about tension around mobilization, with no factual claims that contradict official sources."}
  ],
  techniques:{
    q:"Which technique is the enemy using?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Emotional Amplification", d:"A single local incident is passed off as a nationwide trend", ok:true,
       e:"Right. A local incident is presented as a nationwide trend. Clickbait headlines do the work: “Lviv rises up!”, “Uprising against the TCC begins.” The scale is the only thing the enemy added."},
      {n:"False Symmetry", d:"Treating both sides of a conflict as equally at fault", ok:false,
       e:"No: none of the sources treat the protesters and the TCC as equivalent sides — Veresiuk fully justifies the crowd, and “The Real Deal” fully blames the authorities."},
      {n:"Insinuation", d:"The careful “I'm not saying anything, just think about it” delivery format", ok:false,
       e:"Partially resembles Raspberry Cordial's style, but phrases like “third Maidan” and “pogroms” are direct claims, not careful hints."},
      {n:"Manufacturing Panic", d:"Stoking civilian fear of the authorities and security services", ok:false,
       e:"Fear of the authorities isn't the goal here: Veresiuk and “The Real Deal” aren't threatening a crackdown, they're inflating the scale of the event to a nationwide level."}
    ]
  },
  counters:{
    q:"Choose your countermeasure.",
    opts:[
      {n:"Speed and Facts", d:"An immediate official statement from the CCD, TCC, and Police backed by full body-cam footage; legal accountability for the brawlers and the chat coordinators.", fx:12, best:true,
       e:"Right. Body-cam footage shows how the clash actually started and outcompetes the plants' visual narrative, legal isolation cuts the instigators off from any “popular uprising,” and the voices of soldiers and veterans dismantle the “army vs. the people” frame. The vacuum is closed before the myth can take root."},
      {n:"Mirror Tactics", d:"Launch a large-scale media campaign against “traitors,” “draft dodgers,” and “Kremlin agents,” demanding the harshest possible punishment for the whole crowd.", fx:-12, rep:-15, best:false,
       e:"No: collectively punishing “the whole crowd” repeats the very logic of division — even Budanov's own post calls for a fair response from law enforcement, not for a crackdown."},
      {n:"Rebuttal and Legal Release", d:"The TCC press office publishes an official text document citing specific articles of Ukraine's mobilization law and excerpts from the URPI, dryly explaining the legal grounds for detaining the citizen.", fx:4, best:false,
       e:"Not enough: video of the clash is already spreading online, and a dry text document with no body-cam footage won't outcompete the visual narrative of the leaks."},
      {n:"Shift the Focus", d:"The conflict in Lviv isn't that big a deal. If we flood the information space with front-line successes, stories of heroism, and good news about international aid, people will figure out on their own where the good guys are and where the bad guys are.", fx:2, cons:true, best:false,
       e:"No: silently pivoting to front-line successes doesn't refute the leak's specific claims (“gunfire,” “detained,” “third Maidan”) — they go unanswered."}
    ]
  },
  debrief:"During the clashes in Sykhiv, the enemy used “Emotional Amplification” to spin a local conflict into the start of a “nationwide uprising.” The manipulation works by triggering public fatigue and fear around mobilization, trying to split civil society from the army. By using “Speed and Facts,” we immediately seize the information initiative with body-cam evidence, isolate the instigators through legal channels, and dismantle the enemy's myth through opinion leaders the public actually trusts. The three-question test still applies: is the pain real? can the cause be verified? who benefits?",
  cliff:""
}
,
{
  id:"migrants", title:"MIGRANT WAVE", tech:"Exploitation of Public Fears", badge:"FEARS", node:"WAVE", art:"assets/op_sykhiv.png", /* TODO(Roma): replace with assets/op_migrants.png once the asset is ready */ map:{x:11,y:52},
  brief:"Amid debate over draft law No. 14211, which would simplify residence and work permits for foreigners in Ukraine, and news that a furniture factory in Khust wants to hire 160 Bangladeshi nationals — loud rallies broke out among young people in Kyiv and other cities, protesting against the “ethnic replacement of Ukrainians.”",
  attack:-14,
  feed:[
    {osint:{created:"March 2022", postsMonth:"Fully anonymous channel. Admins hidden. 820,000 subscribers. Reach of this post: 450,000 views in 2 hours, 120 reposts.", avatar:"Stylized trident on a dark background (unchanged since creation)", oldPosts:["Zaluzhnyi is preparing a military coup with British backing.","Western partners are demanding the mobilization age be lowered to 18.","The Oreshnik strike on Bila Tserkva targeted the Bila Tserkva Cargo Aviation Complex (BDAK)."], repostedBy:"Anonymous news aggregators and channels like “Overheard in Odesa,” Typical “Kharkiv.”"}, a:"📡 Citizen", t:"Our source inside the Office of the President says Bankova is in a panic over the youth riots against migrants. The authorities are trying to spin this as a hostile IPSO to shut the kids up, calling the people's protest on Maidan the \"hand of the Kremlin.\"", m:"Mon 18:40", v:"450K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Anonymous Insider"},
    {osint:{created:"May 2026", postsMonth:"340 subscribers, but the post has 150,000 reach and 4,000 reposts", avatar:"Stock photo of a guy in a vyshyvanka, found via reverse image search", nameHistory:"Slava from Ukraine", oldPosts:["The account barely has any history — 95% of posts are reposts of AI-generated tracks and calls to “Everyone to Maidan.”"], repostedBy:"Freshly created accounts with no avatars or bio"}, a:"🐦 @_Slava_UA_89", t:"Posts a TikTok video: His brother is rotting in a trench near Pokrovsk, and tomorrow some foreigner will be sitting in his Chernihiv or Khust taking his wife's job! Listen to this track, every word here is truth! The government sold our country to international corparations. Rise up, Ukraine! Everyone to the rallies if you don't want to wake up in Asia! #NoReplacement #Law14211».", m:"Mon 19:15", v:"150K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Astroturfed Mobilization"},
    {osint:{created:"March 2025", postsMonth:"5-6 posts a month", avatar:"NGO logo: white lettering NUMBERS on a black background", nameHistory:"Official page of NGO “FIGURES” Youth │ Upbringing │ Action", oldPosts:["In February 2026, servicemen from a special unit of Ukraine's Defense Intelligence (GUR) ran a tactical training program for Ukrainian youth in Rivne.","Helped set up a location for the physical rehabilitation and health support of our veterans.","NGO “Steel NATION” together with the guys from NGO “NUMBERS” signed a memorandum of cooperation."], repostedBy:"youth, sports, and nationalist organizations"}, a:"📸 NGO “NUMBERS”", t:"IMMIGRATION ON OUR BLOOD?!❌ Shameful laws bringing in labor migrants to cover a workforce shortage. 😡 While Ukraine loses its best sons and daughters at the front defending its Homeland and its future — laws like this destroy the very essence of what we're fighting for today. Instead of trying to save the lives of our own citizens and creating conditions for foreign volunteers to come straight to the front — we're being replaced in the rear by foreigners who came here to earn money and, of course, will settle in and take root over time.", m:"Mon 20:05", v:"38K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"Patriotic Wrapper"},
    {osint:{created:"May 2013", postsMonth:"Until May 2026 the woman posted 2-3 times a month about seedlings and recipes, wished friends happy birthday, and reposted photos of relatives. In the last 48 hours, 20 identical comments were sent from her account across various Zakarpattia groups.", avatar:"Photo of a middle-aged woman against a background of flowers. Browsing the account's photos confirms she's from Khust."}, a:"👤 Maria Molodyuk · “Native Khust”", t:"People, this is shocking! A friend from the factory confirmed it. They're planning to house these thugs in the forestry college dormitory. Our boys are at war, and here they're bringing in god knows who with a completely different culture, if they even have one… Women are already afraid to go out in the evenings. Why is city hall silent?", m:"Tue 09:30", v:"12K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"Hijacked Account"},
    {osint:{postsMonth:"Public figure, political commentator, frequent guest on Ukrainian TV channels and a regular speaker on YouTube platforms. Personal channel has 180,000 subscribers. The video of this appearance racked up 120,000 views, 8,000 likes, and 2,500 Facebook shares in a day.", oldPosts:["Mobilization to the last Ukrainian: who benefits from wiping out the nation?","Western financial aid never reaches the people — it's stolen at the ministry level.","The government is building roads during wartime: where are our taxes going"], repostedBy:"Anonymous news aggregators, opposition politicians"}, a:"🎬 Mykhailo Chaplenko · shorts", t:"Big business is once again lobbying its interests through the Verkhovna Rada. The new migration initiatives are an attempt by oligarchs to save on wages. Instead of paying Ukrainians decent money during wartime, they're bringing in rightless laborers they can pay pennies. The TikTok music trend and the teenage protests are a natural revolt against capitalist slavery, and there's no need to chalk up people's genuine domestic frustration to some external conspiracy.", m:"Tue 11:50", v:"120K", h:true, tier:"sub", subtype:"IPSO Denial"},
    {osint:{created:"October 2011", postsMonth:"Profile is fully alive and natural. Lots of personal photos from different years, tags from friends and relatives.", avatar:"Personal photo. Reverse image search confirmed it's original.", oldPosts:["Any recommendations for a math tutor for a 13-year-old girl?","They grow up so fast… [photo]","Urgent fundraiser for a pickup truck for the unit my brother serves in."]}, a:"👤 Oksana Melnyk · “Kyiv Moms”", t:"Girls, what is even going on? I read all this stuff in the groups about buses full of migrants, now I'm scared to let my kid go to practice alone in the evening. Has anyone actually seen anything or is it fakes again? My heart is racing from this news.", m:"Tue 12:20", v:"6K", h:false,
     w:"She isn't asserting anything — she's asking: “Has anyone actually seen anything or is it fakes again?” That's a request for verification, not a plant. Compare it to Maria Molodyuk's post: same emotion, same fear — but hers states unverified specifics (“the forestry college dormitory”) as fact. The tell of a hostile post isn't fear, it's specifics with no source. Oksana is the target of this operation, not its instrument. Flag her, and you hit your own side."},
    {osint:{created:"LinkedIn profile has existed since 2015", postsMonth:"5-6 long posts a month", avatar:"Personal photo speaking at a forum", oldPosts:["Changes to draft deferrals for IT workers: pros and cons.","My comment for Forbes Ukraine on corporate governance reform.","support the charity legal marathon in support of the Armed Forces of Ukraine."], repostedBy:"Written in professional language with references to specific articles of the Verkhovna Rada's regulations and EU directives. Reposted by fellow lawyers and HR directors at major companies."}, a:"💼 Taras Shevchuk, legal analyst", t:"Draft law No. 14211 on the employment of foreigners, drafted by the State Migration Service, aims to align Ukrainian legislation with EU law, specifically Directive 2024/1233. The document introduces a \"single permit\" procedure for foreigners' residence and work.", m:"Tue 14:00", v:"18K", h:false,
     w:"A dry recap of the document's contents with a reference to a specific directive. No judgments, no insinuations, nothing emotional. Boring — and that's exactly why it's useful: this is what fills the vacuum of “what does it actually say.”"},
    {osint:{created:"Registered state news agency, website has operated since 2002. Official state media outlet, funded from the budget.", postsMonth:"Over 500,000 unique visitors a day. This story was picked up by 15 leading national media outlets.", avatar:"Agency brand kit, blue-and-yellow styling", oldPosts:["Cabinet of Ministers allocates funds to repair fortifications in border regions","Ukrainian grain export statistics for the first half of the year","Ukrenergo report on restoring a high-voltage line after shelling"], repostedBy:"Official regional administration channels, the Center for Strategic Communications, press officers."}, a:"📰 UkrInform Center", t:"Police recorded spontaneous gatherings of teenagers in Kyiv and Khust. According to the Interior Ministry, public order was not disturbed and there were no detentions. The situation in both cities is under control. Earlier, rumors spread on social media about the arrival of large groups of foreign workers; that information is currently being verified by the relevant agencies.", m:"Tue 16:30", v:"95K", h:false,
     w:"A rebuttal with specifics: no detentions, rumors being checked. Not “everything's under control” with no numbers, but a factual record with a source. The only awkward part is that it came out a day after the leak — a speed problem, not a substance problem."}
  ],
  techniques:{
    q:"What is the enemy layering its narrative onto?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Exploitation of Public Fears", d:"An emotional trigger — xenophobia and fear of “replacement” — is artificially layered onto a real domestic problem", ok:true,
       e:"Right. The wartime labor shortage is real. The draft law is real. The enemy didn't invent anything — it simply covered a real problem with an emotional trigger: xenophobia and fear of “replacement.” The goal is twofold: discredit Ukraine to Western partners as a “radical state” and undermine the economy. The three-question test: is the pain real? can the cause be verified? who benefits from me believing exactly this?"},
      {n:"Discrediting International Support", d:"The enemy pushes the idea that allied aid only worsens Ukraine's situation and prolongs the war", ok:false,
       e:"Reread the feed: only Chaplenko mentions Western aid, and only in passing — “Western sponsors” here is set dressing, not the target. The attack is aimed at foreigners in the rear, not at allies."},
      {n:"Undermining Trust in Official Sources", d:"The enemy tries to convince the audience that state bodies and Ukrainian media systematically hide the truth", ok:false,
       e:"Close, but that's a byproduct, not the core. “Why is city hall silent?” only comes up once. But “we're being replaced,” “wake up in Asia,” “a foreigner will take his job” — that's in four posts out of five. The target is fear, not trust."},
      {n:"Legalizing a War Crime", d:"The enemy justifies its own strikes by shifting responsibility for the consequences onto the Ukrainian side", ok:false,
       e:"Wrong front. There's not a single strike, not a single piece of debris, not a single mention of attacks in this feed. That's the technique from “Debris” and “Vyshneve” — here it simply has nothing to latch onto."}
    ]
  },
  counters:{
    q:"Your move. What do you publish?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Strategic Fact-Checking and Isolating Botfarms", d:"The State Migration Service clarifies the draft law, dry statistics are published, and hacked accounts that spread the panic get blocked", fx:12, best:true,
       e:"Right. Numbers kill a myth better than an argument does: before the war Ukraine issued over 21,000 work permits to foreigners a year, now it's under 10,000. That's a drop by half, not a “wave.” The factory case dates back a year: no permit was ever issued, no foreigner ever arrived. In parallel, hacked accounts like Maria Molodyuk's, which spread the same copy-paste panic, get blocked. Defense against this kind of IPSO isn't arguing with bots — it's speaking in hard numbers and immediate fact-clarification."},
      {n:"Exposing the Source", d:"Identify and publicly reveal exactly who is behind the campaign's spread and which resources coordinate it", fx:4, best:false,
       e:"Partial credit. A network graph is useful — but it won't win back anyone who already believed it. They saw Maria's neighbor-post, not an analysis. The source gets exposed, the fear stays. This is a supplement to the numbers, not a replacement."},
      {n:"Media Counterattack (Exposing the Russian Trail)", d:"Bring in leading media experts for a large-scale breakdown of the technical side of the IPSO: how the GRU made the AI track and inflated view counts among teenagers", fx:-8, best:false,
       e:"Mistake: this scales up the scandal. A breakdown of “how the GRU made the AI track” pushes the track to the top and advertises it — while thousands of teenagers who rallied in good faith hear themselves called agents. Reread post 1: “The authorities are trying to spin this as a hostile IPSO to shut the kids up.” You just did exactly what it predicted."},
      {n:"Placate the Protesters by Taking Their Side", d:"Officials at a press conference reassure the public and promise to look into the situation and conduct an urgent audit of labor conditions", fx:2, rep:-10, cons:true, best:false,
       e:"Mistake: this legitimizes the fake. An audit only makes sense when there's something to audit — and no foreigner ever arrived here. By promising to “look into it,” you're admitting the problem exists. A week later, the absence of audit results becomes proof that “the authorities are hiding something.” Saakyan calls this loud silence in new packaging — you said nothing, but you promised everything."}
    ]
  },
  debrief:"The enemy doesn't always invent a problem from scratch. Russian intelligence services took a real labor shortage in Ukraine and the debate around an EU-integration draft law, then artificially layered xenophobia onto it through AI music and hijacked neighbor accounts. Defense against this kind of IPSO isn't arguing with bots — it's speaking in hard numbers (statistics) and immediate fact-clarification. This operation's main anchor is “a question ≠ a claim.” Maria Molodyuk and Oksana Melnyk are equally scared. But one states unverified specifics, the other asks if it's fake. The tell of a hostile post isn't emotion, it's specifics with no source. And separately: being against the draft law is a legitimate position. Spreading made-up specifics about a dormitory is not legitimate, no matter what side you're on. The three-question test still applies: is the pain real? can the cause be verified? who benefits?",
  cliff:""
}
